<tool id="nexus_eln_builder" name="NeXus ELN builder" version="@TOOL_VERSION@" profile="@PROFILE@">
    <description>from Zenodo metadata and context files</description>
    <macros>
        <import>macros.xml</import>
    </macros>
    <expand macro="requirements_eln"/>
    <required_files>
        <include path="nexus_eln_builder.py"/>
        <include path="nexus_eln_llm_merge.py"/>
        <include path="nexus_llm_input.py"/>
    </required_files>
    <version_command>echo @TOOL_VERSION@</version_command>
    <command detect_errors="exit_code"><![CDATA[
        python '$__tool_directory__/nexus_eln_builder.py'
        '$bundle'
        --rules '$rules'
        --technique '$technique'
        --header '$header'
        #if $answer:
            --answer '$answer'
        #end if
        --eln '$eln'
        --report '$eln_report'
    ]]></command>
    <inputs>
        <param name="bundle" type="data" format="json" label="Context bundle" help="Written by the Zenodo download for NOMAD tool: record metadata and the text of one raw file's context files."/>
        <expand macro="rules_input"/>
        <expand macro="header_input"/>
        <param argument="--answer" type="data" format="markdown,txt" optional="true" label="LLM detection answer" help="Optional. The LLM Hub answer of the detection job (NeXus ELN LLM input, stage detect): technique and scan mode with quotes."/>
        <param argument="--technique" type="text" value="auto" label="Experiment technique" help="auto: from the LLM detection answer, the header markers or the extension, as listed in the rules. Or a technique of the rules, e.g. STM, STS or AFM for pynxtools-spm.">
            <validator type="regex" message="auto, or a technique name (letters and digits)">[A-Za-z0-9_]+</validator>
        </param>
    </inputs>
    <outputs>
        <data name="eln" format="yaml" label="${bundle.element_identifier}: ELN (eln_data.yaml)"/>
        <data name="eln_report" format="json" label="${bundle.element_identifier}: ELN report"/>
    </outputs>
    <tests>
        <!-- Test 01: values from the record and its context files; the user is the harvest's user,
             not the "Operator:" line of a context file. -->
        <test expect_num_outputs="2">
            <param name="bundle" value="bundle_with_context.json" ftype="json"/>
            <param name="rules" value="eln_rules.yaml" ftype="yaml"/>
            <param name="header" value="const_dos_header.json" ftype="json"/>
            <output name="eln" ftype="yaml">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_text text="experiment_technique: STM"/>
                    <has_text text="definition: NXstm"/>
                    <has_text text="identifier_collection: https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.17533355"/>
                    <has_text text="name: magnetic adatom chains on a superconductor"/>
                    <has_text text="scan_mode: constant current"/>
                    <has_text text="Rütten, Lisa M."/>
                    <not_has_text text="&lt;b&gt;"/>
                    <has_text text="- name: Test Person"/>
                    <has_text text="email: test.person@example.org"/>
                    <has_text text="affiliation: Example Institute"/>
                    <has_text text="role: harvested and converted the data"/>
                    <not_has_text text="Jane Doe"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
            <output name="eln_report" ftype="json">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_json_property_with_value property="Sample.name" value="&quot;STM data/readme.txt&quot;"/>
                    <has_json_property_with_value property="User" value="&quot;the harvest's user (work list)&quot;"/>
                    <has_text_matching expression="&quot;missing&quot;: \[\s*\]"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
        </test>
        <!-- Test 02: no context files and no user; user, sample and scan mode are reported missing. -->
        <test expect_num_outputs="2">
            <param name="bundle" value="bundle_without_context.json" ftype="json"/>
            <param name="rules" value="eln_rules.yaml" ftype="yaml"/>
            <param name="header" value="no_header.json" ftype="json"/>
            <output name="eln" ftype="yaml">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_text text="definition: NXsts"/>
                    <not_has_text text="Sample:"/>
                    <not_has_text text="scan_mode:"/>
                    <not_has_text text="User:"/>
                    <has_text text="Not found in the record or its context files: User, Sample.name, scan_mode."/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
            <output name="eln_report" ftype="json">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_text text="&quot;Sample.name&quot;"/>
                    <has_json_property_with_value property="experiment_technique" value="&quot;extension .dat&quot;"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
        </test>
        <!-- Test 03: the technique parameter overrides the extension, e.g. a Nanonis AFM image. -->
        <test expect_num_outputs="2">
            <param name="bundle" value="bundle_with_context.json" ftype="json"/>
            <param name="rules" value="eln_rules.yaml" ftype="yaml"/>
            <param name="header" value="const_dos_header.json" ftype="json"/>
            <param name="technique" value="AFM"/>
            <output name="eln" ftype="yaml">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_text text="experiment_technique: AFM"/>
                    <has_text text="definition: NXafm"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
            <output name="eln_report" ftype="json">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_json_property_with_value property="experiment_technique" value="&quot;tool parameter&quot;"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
        </test>
        <!-- Test 04: a technique the rules do not know fails the job. -->
        <test expect_failure="true">
            <param name="bundle" value="bundle_with_context.json" ftype="json"/>
            <param name="rules" value="eln_rules.yaml" ftype="yaml"/>
            <param name="header" value="const_dos_header.json" ftype="json"/>
            <param name="technique" value="XPS"/>
            <assert_stderr>
                <has_text text="Unknown technique 'XPS'; the rules file has: STM, STS, AFM"/>
            </assert_stderr>
        </test>
        <!-- Test 05: Nanonis AFM .sxm without an answer: the header marker wins over the extension
             (.sxm: STM); the conflict is reported. -->
        <test expect_num_outputs="2">
            <param name="bundle" value="bundle_afm.json" ftype="json"/>
            <param name="rules" value="eln_rules.yaml" ftype="yaml"/>
            <param name="header" value="afm_header.json" ftype="json"/>
            <output name="eln" ftype="yaml">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_text text="experiment_technique: AFM"/>
                    <not_has_text text="scan_mode:"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
            <output name="eln_report" ftype="json">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_json_property_with_value property="experiment_technique" value="&quot;header marker 'Frequency_Shift'&quot;"/>
                    <has_json_property_with_value property="extension" value="&quot;STM&quot;"/>
                    <has_json_property_with_value property="conflict" value="true"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
        </test>
        <!-- Test 06: a marker on a gwyddionpy header (JSON) of a Bruker .FLT file (pynxtools-spm test data). -->
        <test expect_num_outputs="2">
            <param name="bundle" value="bundle_with_context.json" ftype="json"/>
            <param name="rules" value="eln_rules.yaml" ftype="yaml"/>
            <param name="header" value="flt_header.json" ftype="json"/>
            <output name="eln" ftype="yaml">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_text text="definition: NXafm"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
            <output name="eln_report" ftype="json">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_json_property_with_value property="experiment_technique" value="&quot;header marker 'Mode: Peak Force Tapping'&quot;"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
        </test>
        <!-- Test 07: hand-written detection answer with quotes from the readme: technique and scan mode kept. -->
        <test expect_num_outputs="2">
            <param name="bundle" value="bundle_afm.json" ftype="json"/>
            <param name="rules" value="eln_rules.yaml" ftype="yaml"/>
            <param name="header" value="afm_header.json" ftype="json"/>
            <param name="answer" value="answer_detect_afm.md" ftype="markdown"/>
            <output name="eln" ftype="yaml">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_text text="experiment_technique: AFM"/>
                    <has_text text="scan_mode: tapping mode"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
            <output name="eln_report" ftype="json">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_json_property_with_value property="experiment_technique" value="&quot;LLM detection (4_readme.txt)&quot;"/>
                    <has_json_property_with_value property="scan_mode" value="&quot;LLM detection (4_readme.txt)&quot;"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
        </test>
        <!-- Test 08: a found quote wins over the extension (.sxm: STM); a scan mode of another
             technique is dropped. -->
        <test expect_num_outputs="2">
            <param name="bundle" value="bundle_17202182.json" ftype="json"/>
            <param name="rules" value="eln_rules.yaml" ftype="yaml"/>
            <param name="header" value="T190613_004_header.json" ftype="json"/>
            <param name="answer" value="answer_detect_sts.md" ftype="markdown"/>
            <output name="eln" ftype="yaml">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_text text="definition: NXsts"/>
                    <not_has_text text="scan_mode:"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
            <output name="eln_report" ftype="json">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_json_property_with_value property="reason" value="&quot;not_allowed for STS&quot;"/>
                    <has_json_property_with_value property="conflict" value="true"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
        </test>
        <!-- Test 09: a quote that is in no source is dropped; the extension decides. -->
        <test expect_num_outputs="2">
            <param name="bundle" value="bundle_with_context.json" ftype="json"/>
            <param name="rules" value="eln_rules.yaml" ftype="yaml"/>
            <param name="header" value="const_dos_header.json" ftype="json"/>
            <param name="answer" value="answer_detect_no_quote.md" ftype="markdown"/>
            <output name="eln" ftype="yaml">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_text text="experiment_technique: STM"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
            <output name="eln_report" ftype="json">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_json_property_with_value property="reason" value="&quot;quote_not_found&quot;"/>
                    <has_json_property_with_value property="experiment_technique" value="&quot;extension .sxm&quot;"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
        </test>
        <!-- Test 10: the fixed answer the workflow puts in place of a failed detection job. -->
        <test expect_num_outputs="2">
            <param name="bundle" value="bundle_with_context.json" ftype="json"/>
            <param name="rules" value="eln_rules.yaml" ftype="yaml"/>
            <param name="header" value="const_dos_header.json" ftype="json"/>
            <param name="answer" value="answer_llm_failed.md" ftype="markdown"/>
            <output name="eln" ftype="yaml">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_text text="experiment_technique: STM"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
            <output name="eln_report" ftype="json">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_json_property_with_value property="status" value="&quot;llm_failed&quot;"/>
                    <has_json_property_with_value property="experiment_technique" value="&quot;extension .sxm&quot;"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
        </test>
    </tests>
    <help format="markdown"><![CDATA[
**What it does**

Builds the ELN (YAML) that a pynxtools reader plugin, e.g.
[pynxtools-spm](https://github.com/FAIRmat-NFDI/pynxtools-spm), needs next to a raw file. It reads
one **context bundle** from the Zenodo download for NOMAD tool: the Zenodo record metadata and the
text of the raw file's context files (readme, notes). The **ELN rules** of the plugin list the
techniques, their NeXus definitions, raw file extensions and header markers.

-----

**Where the values come from**

- `experiment_technique` and `definition`: the first of
  1. the **Experiment technique** parameter, if not `auto`;
  2. the **LLM detection answer**, if its quote is found in a source file (header, record text,
     context files);
  3. the `header_markers` of the rules (regular expressions on the **raw file header**), if only one
     technique's markers match;
  4. the raw file's extension, as listed in the rules (for pynxtools-spm: `.sxm` → STM, `.dat` → STS,
     `.spm` → AFM, ...).

  The report lists every candidate and `conflict: true` when they differ.
- `identifier_collection`, `citeID`, `experiment_description`: the record's DOI, creators, title
  and description.
- `Sample/name`, `Sample/description`, `scan_mode`: lines such as `Sample: Au(111)` or
  `Scan mode: constant current` in the context files. Else `scan_mode` from the LLM detection
  answer, if its quote is found and it is an allowed value of the technique.
- `User`: the person who runs the harvest (name, email, affiliation from the work list), with the
  role "harvested and converted the data". People named in the dataset files are not users; the
  Zenodo creators are in `citeID`.

Nothing is guessed. Fields that were not found are listed at the top of the ELN and in the
**ELN report**, together with the file each value came from.
    ]]></help>
    <citations>
        <expand macro="citation_pynxtools_spm"/>
    </citations>
    <expand macro="creators"/>
</tool>
